     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single dose of 1600 mg is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day and a common regimen.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day and typical for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the absolute ceiling, and I'd suggest adding a GI protection plan and a short duration.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd recommend confirming with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you pick a regimen, I'll enter it right away."
      }
