       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I'm not aware of any indication that supports it. The extra dose adds risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events without adding analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the effect plateaus well below that level.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum dose, and I can add a note about GI protection and a short duration.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day).\n\nIf you have a specific reason to go beyond the labeled maximum, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, please discuss it with pharmacy or your attending. The order can be entered through that channel with documented rationale and monitoring. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
